        "description": "## Overview\n[@hono/node-server](https://www.npmjs.org/package/@hono/node-server) is a Node.js Adapter for Hono\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Double Decoding of the Same Data via the `serveStatic` middleware in `src/serve-static.ts`, where a percent-encoded path sequence in a request URL is decoded by `tryDecodeURI` before the path traversal check is applied. An attacker can supply a percent-encoded traversal sequence (e.g. `%2e%2e`) in the request path to escape the intended static file root and read arbitrary files from the server's filesystem.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `@hono/node-server` to version 2.1.3 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/honojs/node-server/security/advisories/GHSA-rmxm-3fg6-px4f)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/honojs/node-server/commit/982179278529d5673812116b042829f27794966f)\n",
