        "description": "## Overview\n[minimatch](https://www.npmjs.com/package/minimatch) is a minimal matching utility.\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Asymmetric Resource Consumption (Amplification) in the `firstPhasePreProcess` method, where the `**/..` transform clones a `globParts` entry and pushes the clone back onto the same array inside a `do...while (didSomething)` fixpoint loop. An attacker can exhaust CPU and memory by supplying a glob pattern whose `**/..` sequences regenerate entries during preprocessing, which `secondPhasePreProcess` then compares in an O(n^2) pairwise `partsMatch` pass over the expanded set. Exploitation requires the pattern to be parsed with `optimizationLevel` set to 2 or higher.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `minimatch` to version 11.0.1 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/isaacs/minimatch/security/advisories/GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/isaacs/minimatch/commit/77a0f5c4b80bdc641c3c930a1d9edf5ad2db57f8)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/isaacs/minimatch/releases/tag/v11.0.1)\n",
