        "description": "## Overview\n[@intlify/core-base](https://www.npmjs.org/package/@intlify/core-base) is a @intlify/core-base\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Improper Encoding or Escaping of Output via the `escapeParams` function in `packages/core-base/src/translate.ts`, when a translation call passes both list and named interpolation values simultaneously. The original logic used `else if` to escape named values, meaning that when a list argument is also present, named values are never passed through `escapeHtml`. An attacker who controls a named interpolation value can inject unescaped HTML into the rendered output, enabling a cross-site scripting attack.\n\n**Note:** This is only exploitable when the `escapeParameter` option is explicitly set to `true`.\n## PoC\n```js\nimport { createI18n } from 'vue-i18n'\n\nconst i18n = createI18n({\n  legacy: false,\n  locale: 'en',\n  escapeParameter: true,\n  messages: {\n    en: { withList: '{0} {name}', withoutList: '{name}' }\n  }\n})\nconst t = i18n.global.t\n\nt('withoutList', { name: '<b>x</b>' })\n// &lt;b&gt;x&lt;&#x2F;b&gt;      escaped\n\nt('withList', ['a'], { named: { name: '<b>x</b>' } })\n// a <b>x</b>                   not escaped (v11.4.13)\n```\n\n**Note:** The PoC uses vue-i18n with `escapeParameter: true` and demonstrates that named values are not escaped when a list argument is also passed.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `@intlify/core-base` to version 12.0.0-alpha.5, 11.4.14 or higher.\n## References\n- [GitHub Advisory](https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n/security/advisories/GHSA-8rc2-428q-7ww3)\n- [GitHub Commit](https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n/commit/d657ce8f4b3b6b198a8f6e3d09e2b57a5d019fb8)\n- [GitHub PR](https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n/pull/2680)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n/releases/tag/v11.4.14)\n- [GitHub Release](https://github.com/intlify/vue-i18n/releases/tag/v12.0.0-alpha.5)\n",
